ven-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Nour</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Candida peritonitis: A rare complication following early dislodgement of percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy tube</article-title><source>J Pediatr Child Health</source><year>2006</year><volume>42</volume><fpage>145</fpage><lpage>6</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Guloglu</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Taviloglu</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Alimoglu</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Colon injury following percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy tube insertion</article-title><source>J Laparoendosc Adv Surg Tech A</source><year>2003</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>69</fpage><lpage>72</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12676027</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Roozrokh</surname><given-names>HC</given-names></name><name><surname>Ripepi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Stahlfeld</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Gastrocolocutaneous Fistula as a complication of peg tube placement</article-title><source>Surg Endosc</source><year>2002</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>538</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11928047</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>